    logo: "/logos/capacities.png",
    stage: "",
    round: null,
    summary: "Capacities is a note-taking and knowledge management app that organizes your ideas as connected objects instead of files and folders. Available free on Mac, Windows, Linux, iOS, and Android. Capacities turns your ideas into connected objects, not files buried in folders. Link anything to anything, and find what you need the moment you need it. You read, research, meet, and think all day. But when you need that one insight, that one connection? Gone. Meeting notes, article highlights, project ideas, fleeting thoughts. They're scattered across apps, docs, and messages. When you need something, you end up searching five places. You read something last month that's relevant to today's project. You know it exists. But your tools treat every note as an island, so the connection stays in your head or gets lost. Where does this go? What folder? What tag? You spend more time filing than thinking. The tool that was supposed to help has become overhead. They were designed for computers, not humans. Files and folders made sense in 1984. Your brain doesn't work that way. Neither should your notes. Your brain doesn't think in folders. It thinks in things —people, books, ideas, projects. And it connects them naturally. We call these objects. In Capacities, everything you care about becomes an object. A person. A book you're reading. A project you're working on. An idea you want to explore. Objects have structure. They have properties. And they connect to each other creating a living network",
