    summary: "Learn about Airbnb's founders, story, and global community of hosts and travelers. Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5.5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2.5 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays, experiences, and services that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way. The Airbed & Breakfast website launches in time for the Democratic National Convention and gets 80 bookings. Airbnb launches Payments, our bespoke payments platform which in 2019 processed about $70 billion in guest and host transactions in over 40 currencies. Airbnb officially changes our name from Airbed & Breakfast to Airbnb and expands beyond rooms to offer apartments, whole homes, and vacation rentals. In response to Hurricane Sandy, Airbnb partners with New York City to house displaced residents and launches our Disaster Relief Tool. Airbnb opens our 888 Brannan Street HQ, a few blocks from our first listing on Rausch Street. Airbnb launches Experiences, a selection of curated activities that immerse travelers in local communities. Airbnb launches Frontline Stays to safely house medical workers and other first responders during the COVID-19 pandemic. Airbnb launches Online Experiences in response to our hosts needing a way to make up for lost earnings during the pandemic. Airbnb launches our Enhanced Cleaning Protocol",
